---
import CommercialLayout from '../layouts/CommercialLayout.astro';
import WorkflowSpecimen from '../components/services/WorkflowSpecimen.astro';
import BriefForm from '../components/services/BriefForm.astro';
import { workflowOffers } from '../data/serviceOffers';
import {
  organizationSchema,
  websiteSchema,
  professionalServiceSchema
} from '../utils/jsonld';
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Home"
  description="Toledo Technologies repairs, builds, and checks the handoffs between websites and business tools. Fixed scope, inspectable tests, and written delivery."
  jsonLd={[organizationSchema(), websiteSchema(), professionalServiceSchema()]}
  pageClass="commercial-home"
>
  <div class="commercial-shell">
    <section class="commercial-hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <div class="commercial-hero__copy">
        <h1 id="home-title">
          The form was submitted. Did the work reach the right place?
        </h1>
        <p class="commercial-lede">
          Toledo Technologies repairs and builds the handoffs between your
          website and your business tools. Clear scope, inspectable tests, and
          ongoing checks for workflows we support.
        </p>
        <div class="commercial-actions">
          <a class="commercial-action" href="/brief/?source=home&service=unsure"
            >Describe your workflow</a
          >
          <a class="commercial-action commercial-action--text" href="#specimen"
            >Inspect an example</a
          >
        </div>
        <p class="commercial-meta">
          Work handled in writing · Local businesses and agency partners welcome
        </p>
      </div>
      <WorkflowSpecimen compact />
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Three signs the handoff deserves a test.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          The website can look healthy while the operating path behind it is
          fragile. Start with the observable failure, not a platform overhaul.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="symptom-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Someone has to check the inbox.</strong><p>
            A submission exists, but nobody can prove its destination or
            ownership.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Retries create duplicate work.</strong><p>
            The same request can become two records, two alerts, or two customer
            replies.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A tool changed quietly.</strong><p>
            The form still says “sent” after a field, permission, or downstream
            rule stopped matching.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section" id="offers">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>One workflow. One accepted result.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          These offers cover a single supported handoff. Larger websites,
          software, discovery, and existing fixed products remain available as
          separate work.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="offer-ledger">
        {
          workflowOffers.map((offer) => (
            <article class="offer-row">
              <div>
                <>
                  <h3>{offer.name}</h3>
                  <p class="offer-price">{offer.price}</p>
                </>
              </div>
              <p>{offer.summary}</p>
              <div>
                <>
                  <p>{offer.delivered}</p>
                  <p class="offer-boundary">Boundary: {offer.boundary}</p>
                </>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="commercial-actions">
        <a class="commercial-action commercial-action--text" href="/workflows/"
          >Read the full workflow terms</a
        ><a class="commercial-action commercial-action--text" href="/services/"
          >Route a different problem</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Evidence includes the path that fails.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          A green happy-path screenshot is not acceptance. The record names the
          input, committed result, duplicate behavior, and a rejected case.
        </p>
      </div>
      <WorkflowSpecimen anchorId="specimen" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="audience-split">
        <article>
          <h3>For a business owner</h3><p>
            Describe the result the business needs. We reply with fit, access
            needs, scope, price, and an acceptance test before paid work starts.
          </p><a href="/brief/?source=home-direct">Send a direct brief</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>For an agency partner</h3><p>
            Keep the client relationship while permissions, attribution,
            reviewer roles, and delivery evidence remain explicit.
          </p><a href="/partner/">Read the partner boundaries</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>The whole purchase happens in writing.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          Automation may assist implementation and routine correspondence.
          Toledo Technologies LLC remains the accountable supplier.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="process-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Send a short brief.</strong><p>
            Name the intended result, current failure, and systems involved.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fit is confirmed.</strong><p>
            Unsupported or unbounded work is declined or routed to the right
            discovery.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Accept the scope.</strong><p>
            You receive price, access needs, acceptance checks, and payment
            terms before work starts.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Review the evidence.</strong><p>
            Acceptance happens in the agreed nonproduction environment. After
            verified production handoff, the accepted scope has a 14-day
            correction window; a deliberately deferred handoff is recorded in
            writing.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Sometimes the business needs its own tool.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          A bounded dashboard, reviewed document process, quote-preparation
          tool, or staff knowledge assistant can be the right scope when
          existing tools and a single workflow are not enough. Custom work is
          separately quoted, uses the same one-project capacity, and keeps a
          named human approver.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="commercial-actions">
        <a class="commercial-action" href="/custom-tools/"
          >Explore custom business tools</a
        ><a
          class="commercial-action commercial-action--text"
          href="/brief/?source=home-custom&service=custom"
          >Describe the internal problem</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Useful boundaries before you write.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary
            >Does Workflow Repair include diagnosis of an unknown problem?</summary
          ><p>
            No. Repair requires one reproducible failure in a supported
            workflow. When the cause or system boundary is unknown, the existing
            $1,200 Integration Triage is a separate diagnostic engagement and
            has no automatic credit toward Repair.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Care guarantee every real inquiry is delivered?</summary
          ><p>
            No. Care checks the registered workflow using read-only signals
            where supported and authorized synthetic tests. It is not 24/7
            response, an uptime SLA, or a guarantee that every real customer
            submission is observed.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can this include a dashboard or internal tool?</summary><p>
            Sometimes, as separately scoped custom work. A bounded tool needs
            one problem, one approver, a data boundary, and an acceptance test.
            It is not included in Workflow Setup or Care.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="commercial-shell">
    <BriefForm source="home" context="Homepage workflow inquiry" />
  </div>
</CommercialLayout>
